      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s1",
      "source_id": "6320eebe-9286-4879-af69-bed939ca44b2",
      "text": "Given your current setup—a basic telescope and a phone app for tracking—it sounds like you're ready for a \"best-effort\" session rather than a perfectly planned one.\n\nIf the clouds remain persistent and don't budge, my suggestion would be to *change your location*.\n\n*   **Geographic Shift:** If your current location is obscured, the most immediate 'Plan B' is a 10-minute drive to the nearest *higher elevation* or a **\"less-populated\" location** (like a less-developed area or a hilltop) to find a gap in the clouds or better viewing angles. \n*   **The 'Quick Check' Strategy:** Instead of waiting for a clear sky, use your phone's \"weather\" features—some apps allow you to \"predict\" cloud movement by checking satellite imagery. You don't need a perfect clear night; even 30 minutes of clear, high-quality viewing is better than nothing at all.\n\n**Since your primary goal is to catch the *maximum* number of visible events, here's a refined tip:**\n\n1.  **Time the \"Best Window\":** If your phone app is showing a specific window for the shower, mark it"
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s2",
      "source_id": "0e6841aa-afa3-4669-9e45-aa1024bc59ea",
      "text": "I'll try moving to a nearby hilltop if the clouds don't clear in the next hour. It's not too far, and I've got the app to check the forecast on the go. I'll let you know if it works out."
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s3",
      "source_id": "061fba13-1136-41c7-b593-5edae80ce7ef",
      "text": "\"Sounds like you're being very proactive about the weather! Good luck with your search! Let me know how the night goes and if the 'quick-scan\" approach pays off. I hope you find a clear window to capture those meteors!\""
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "external",
      "slot": "s4",
      "source_id": "c15c7071-07ea-4458-b0a1-62d9b35bb3fd",
      "text": "Thanks, I appreciate the support. I'll keep you posted, but if the sky stays cloudy, I might just end up stargazing from my backyard instead. It's not ideal, but I'll make the best of it."
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s5",
      "source_id": "3dee04cc-cd64-4cb2-b853-6a9cc552e0d0",
      "text": "Sounds like you have a solid contingency plan! Sometimes the best \"stargazing\" is just enjoying the atmosphere and maybe catching a bit of ambient light or just enjoying the silence of the night, which is a great experience in itself.\n\nLet me know how it goes, or if you decide to try a different location!"
    }
  ]
